---
import { trustPages } from "../data/trust-pages";
import TrustPageLayout from "../layouts/TrustPageLayout.astro";

const page = trustPages.about;
---

<TrustPageLayout page={page} currentKey="about">
  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    The intended audience is small-business decision makers who select, manage,
    secure, or govern technology without a large specialist team.
  </p>
  <h2>What each guide should deliver</h2>
  <p>
    Published articles identify a concrete business problem, keep technology
    central to the decision, define the intended reader, state a useful outcome,
    and provide traceable sources. Product promotion and unsupported certainty
    are outside that scope.
  </p>
  <h2>Publication identity and scope</h2>
  <p>
    The publication name does not establish a person, company, team,
    professional credential, physical location, or record of hands-on product
    testing. The separate <a href="/publisher/">publisher page</a> states the current
    identity boundary.
  </p>
</TrustPageLayout>
